PRE-EXISTING (not introduced by NEARS-1869) — same non-JSON-200 crash class, wallet money path.
File: UserApp/lib/features/loyalty/domain/repositories/loyalty_repository.dart
Function: pointToWallet() — proven BYTE-IDENTICAL base 066fcc95 -> HEAD ee15b0d3 (sha256 9d63a648...)

  Future<ResponseModel> pointToWallet({int? point}) async {
    ResponseModel responseModel;
    Response response = await apiClient.postData(AppConstants.loyaltyPointTransferUri, {"point": point});
    if (response.statusCode == 200) {
      responseModel = ResponseModel(true, response.body['message']);   // <-- unguarded index on a non-Map body
    } else {
      responseModel = ResponseModel(false, response.statusText);
    }
    return responseModel;
  }

NEARS-1869 widened the sibling _getLoyaltyTransactionList gate to `statusCode == 200 && response.body is Map`.
pointToWallet still indexes response.body['message'] behind a bare `statusCode == 200`, so a captive-portal /
hostile-proxy HTML 200 on /api/v1/customer/loyalty-point/point-transfer throws the same
  type 'String' is not a subtype of type 'Map<String, dynamic>'
on a MONEY path, with no AppLogger.failure emitter (silent-failure path).

NOT live-reproducible in this run: the Convert CTA is config-gated behind `exchangeRate > 0`
(loyalty_card_widget.dart:100) and the shared dev DB has business_settings
loyalty_point_exchange_rate = 0, so the CTA never renders. Opening it needs a business_settings
mutation, which the QA read-only DB rule forbids. Static finding + config evidence only.
Out of NEARS-1869's AC scope -> regression lane, does not block this ticket.
